<div class="mb-12" data-reveal>
  <h2 class="mb-4 text-[26px] font-semibold leading-[1.2] tracking-tight text-[#111827] md:text-[30px]">Why it mattered</h2>
  <p class="mb-5 text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">
    A tighter spreadsheet or a stricter checklist process would still have relied on someone remembering to check the right sheet at the right time. Mach24 Orbital needed the dependencies themselves to surface automatically, before a person had to go looking &mdash; which is the difference between finding a conflict during review and finding it a day before launch.
  </p>
  <blockquote class="border-l-4 border-[#76B900] pl-4 text-[15px] italic leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280]">
    &ldquo;A missed dependency doesn't show up as an error message. It shows up as a scrubbed launch. We needed the system to catch what a checklist can't.&rdquo;
    <span class="mt-2 block not-italic text-[13px] text-navy-400">&mdash; Launch Operations Lead, Mach24 Orbital</span>
  </blockquote>
</div>

<div class="rounded-2xl border border-navy-100/60 bg-white p-8 shadow-subtle" data-reveal>
  <blockquote class="mb-4 text-[19px] italic leading-relaxed text-[#111827]">
    &ldquo;Launch prep used to mean chasing status updates across five different teams. Now we see the whole readiness picture in one place, and we catch conflicts early enough to actually do something about them.&rdquo;
  </blockquote>
  <p class="text-[14px] text-[#6B7280]">
    <strong class="font-semibold text-[#111827]">Launch Operations Lead</strong><br>
    Mach24 Orbital
  </p>
</div>

